<title>GREECE: Greek FRN auction produces cut-off price of 99.92.</title>
<headline>Greek FRN auction produces cut-off price of 99.92.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following information on the Greek auction of seven-year floaters was made available by the Bank of Greece.</p>
<p>					FRNs</p>
<p>   ISSUE DATE		  30 June, 1997</p>
<p>   TERM			    7-years</p>
<p>   FORMULA		   12-mth T-bill +0.80%</p>
<p>   12-MTH T-BILL		 9.60%</p>
<p>   FACE VALUE		 1.0 million drachmas</p>
<p>   MIN ACCEPTED PRICE	  999,200</p>
<p>   AVER ACCEPTED PRICE	1,000,583.79</p>
<p>   MAX  ACCEPTED PRICE	1,004,000</p>
<p>   AMOUNT COMPETITIVE	   150 bln drachmas</p>
<p>   AMOUNT NON-COMPETITIVE	45 bln drachmas</p>
<p>--Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
